WEBVTT

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:17.500
Yasunari, come here.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:22.040
I have something for you.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:23.410
Give me your hand.

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.830
Say something.

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:38.500
I'm telling you just in case,
but I didn't draw this out of spite.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.200
It's a charm.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.000
Really?

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:47.870
I want to get mad, but it's true
that I haven't been the nicest to you...

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:49.450
But this is different!

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:51.000
This is a <i>tanuki</i>!

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:52.830
<i>Tanuki?</i>

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:56.910
I'd draw this on my hand
before a match and wish...

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:59.660
...that I'd weasel past everyone.

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:01.660
I didn't know you did things like that.

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:04.000
I kept it a secret from you.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.500
Do you know why?

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:12.200
I didn't want a rival like you
to find out about my secret charm.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:15.830
Back when I was still playing,
I was afraid of you.

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:18.370
I felt like you'd surpass me
at any given moment.

00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:21.330
Really...?

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:25.000
Yeah. But I escaped!

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.160
You lost your chance to beat me forever!

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:29.580
Too bad for you!

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:34.790
But as an apology, I'm going
to give this to you, Yasunari.

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:38.750
You'll be fine for sure.

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:41.950
I never played poorly
on the days I drew this charm.

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:46.790
Wow! Natsu-<i>san </i>is being mean to his junior again!
And right before a match, too!

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:48.620
Hey! That's not it at all!

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:27.910
"When watching rugby in winter,
dress as warmly as possible!!"

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:31.120
Shingyouji.

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:37.540
There's no wind today.
I bet we'll have a good match.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:41.910
Has Natsusa been that way the whole time?

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:45.370
I mean, just like he was on the bullet train?

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:47.540
--Yes.
--I see.

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:51.620
It feels really strange
that he's acting so normally.

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:54.580
He should have come to our university.

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:59.000
I could have given him a lot
of support along the way.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:03.410
I mean, the two of you don't talk much
when you're together, right?

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:06.910
Or sometimes it looks like Natsusa
is having one-sided conversations.

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:12.000
That's why I always worry if you're
giving him the support he needs.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.750
They don't always need to exchange words
because they're so close, Madoka-<i>san</i>.

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:17.580
Whoa! That scared me!

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:18.540
When did you get here?

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:19.700
Just now.

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:23.200
You always bully Seiichirou
the moment you have a chance!

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:25.830
What? I'm not bullying him.

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:28.950
More importantly, Ibuki.
Watch out for injuries today.

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:29.870
What?

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:32.200
Is your little brother really doing that bad?

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:36.040
Well, this morning, I made
a comment that sheep were cute

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:40.700
and he responded with,
"Huh? Did you say kill Ibuki?"

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:42.660
That's a huge jump in words!

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:46.410
Well, let's both try our best today.

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:54.120
Huh? Are you irritated?

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:55.500
I'm fine.

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:59.410
I'm not as upset as I was when
you suddenly quit playing rugby.

00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:02.200
Huh?! You were <i>that </i>pissed off?!

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:03.540
I was.

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:07.410
If Natsu didn't go to beat you up,
I was going to do it myself.

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:08.410
That's scary!

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:11.660
I've never been able to tell
what you're thinking!

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:14.620
I'm so glad it was Natsusa!

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:17.830
Ibuki-<i>san</i>, you are surprisingly dense.

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:22.660
Seiichirou-<i>san</i>, you are surprisingly naive.

00:05:34.540 --> 00:05:36.250
Taisei.

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:39.790
Mako-<i>san</i>, I...

00:05:39.790 --> 00:05:42.160
I'm depending on you, starting player!

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:45.500
You are a junior that I'm proud of!

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:48.500
Yes.

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:53.540
--Hey.
--Yes!

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:54.700
Taping.

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:57.620
Yes! I'll call for Natsusa-<i>san</i>!

00:05:57.620 --> 00:05:59.450
I think he's doing Seiichirou-<i>san</i>'s right now--!

00:05:59.450 --> 00:06:01.120
I want you to do it.

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:03.330
Huh? Me?!

00:06:03.330 --> 00:06:05.830
But I've never done taping for a match.

00:06:05.830 --> 00:06:07.120
Well...

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:11.290
I did really well when you did
the taping during practice last time...

00:06:11.290 --> 00:06:13.790
Oh! Th-Then, allow me to...

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:17.200
Uh, it's not something
to be that nervous about...

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:19.500
Um! Um!

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:21.290
You don't have to do it that perfectly.

00:06:21.290 --> 00:06:25.120
I do! Stable taping leads to a stable mentality!

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:26.200
What are you talking about?

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:27.910
My words of wisdom!

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:30.540
Your words?

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:31.750
Yes!

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:39.200
I've said everything I want to say
and have done everything I can.

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:41.750
However, I would like to confirm
with all of you once more.

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:46.500
We will win this match and
go to nationals. Understood?

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:48.370
Yes!

00:06:48.370 --> 00:06:49.290
Who are we?

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:50.830
Doushisha!

00:06:52.950 --> 00:06:54.660
Everyone, wait.

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:57.200
Go and win.

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:02.370
My heroes.

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:06.580
Got it.

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:10.620
"Kansai University Rugby A League"
"Doushisha University
vs
Koufuuin University"

00:07:26.330 --> 00:07:28.250
Feeling good.

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:36.540
That aggression is great.

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:44.160
Koufuuin. Number 10.

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:45.160
Failure to release the ball.

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:46.250
All right!

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:48.120
As expected of Su-<i>san</i>!

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.410
So dangerous!

00:08:14.250 --> 00:08:15.330
Just a bit more!

00:08:15.330 --> 00:08:16.330
Go!

00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:29.200
Knock-on.

00:08:31.950 --> 00:08:37.660
Ibuki. I've been telling you since high school.

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:39.830
Don't go against me.

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:43.120
What are you doing?!

00:08:47.620 --> 00:08:49.870
Ethan, stop it.

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:56.370
Is Ibuki-<i>san </i>all right?

00:08:56.370 --> 00:08:59.040
That was right in the stomach...

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:01.330
What the hell are you getting a knock-on for.

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:02.620
So strict!

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:05.500
Yasunari-<i>kun</i>.

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:09.120
You've grown so much
since the last time I saw you.

00:09:15.410 --> 00:09:17.790
Hey. Is Ibuki all right?

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:20.200
I'm the one that's not all right.

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:22.250
Let's go crush the scrum.

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:24.620
Yeah, leave it to us.

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:32.160
Kazutaka-<i>san </i>isn't joining the scrum...

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:35.000
Looks like he's switching positions
with their number 10.

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:38.620
That's the first time Koufuuin
has done something like that.

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:41.120
Crouch!

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:42.790
Bind! Set!

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:12.040
In other words, they're planning
to crush Ibuki-<i>senpai </i>completely.

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:19.750
"Doushisha"                         "Koufuuin"

00:10:20.790 --> 00:10:22.200
"Doushisha"                          "Koufuuin"

00:10:24.950 --> 00:10:26.120
"Doushisha"                           "Koufuuin"

00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:28.580
"Doushisha"                           "Koufuuin"

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:31.620
A difference of 14 points...

00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:35.370
They seem hot-blooded,
but they're actually very rational.

00:10:35.370 --> 00:10:37.910
Kotori's passes are still lacking.

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:40.000
Ethan is also bad with passes.

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:43.750
Even so, we've managed to get by
because of Ibuki's skills.

00:10:43.750 --> 00:10:46.250
Now that he's getting completely crushed...

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:50.080
The forwards and backs will get
completely out of sync with each other.

00:10:57.290 --> 00:10:58.410
This guy!

00:11:03.870 --> 00:11:05.000
Try!

00:11:08.370 --> 00:11:12.290
Touma! As expected! Good job!

00:11:12.290 --> 00:11:13.910
Yes.

00:11:13.910 --> 00:11:18.250
Who is that player? I've never seen him before.

00:11:18.250 --> 00:11:19.080
He is a first year student!

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:21.830
"Touma Okumura"
This is his first time playing in a league match

00:11:21.830 --> 00:11:23.790
"Touma Okumura"
so nobody had been marking him.

00:11:23.790 --> 00:11:26.540
It looks like he played
basketball in high school.

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:27.500
Basketball?!

00:11:27.500 --> 00:11:30.250
It must have been Madoka-<i>san</i>.

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:33.750
It's not just his strategic plays
that make him scary.

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:36.250
It's his ability to raise back players.

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:37.290
Huh?

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:40.620
Madoka-<i>san </i>was the one who trained me.

00:11:40.620 --> 00:11:44.750
Sei doesn't get along with
Madoka-<i>san </i>for some reason,

00:11:44.750 --> 00:11:47.450
but Madoka-<i>san </i>still coached him indirectly.

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:55.290
Even Yasunari, who didn't share any
years of high school with Madoka-<i>san</i>,

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:59.830
got some coaching from him during
his visits back home during break.

00:11:59.830 --> 00:12:04.700
He pulls people from other clubs
if he takes a liking to them.

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:07.160
So he's doing that at his university...

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:13.370
It's the reason the teams that Madoka-<i>san</i>
plays in all have really strong backs.

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:28.080
We're in a lot more trouble than I expected.

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:34.000
We can't do anything at all...

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:37.040
Is it me? Is this all my fault?

00:12:37.040 --> 00:12:38.160
Kureha!

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:47.500
I... I've got to do something about this!

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:50.620
You're going to play rugby? No way!

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:53.950
If you were more manly, sure...

00:12:53.950 --> 00:12:59.540
You have such a small frame, so hurry up
and come to terms with what you can do!

00:12:59.540 --> 00:13:01.450
You've got to be kidding me!

00:13:01.450 --> 00:13:03.620
I've got to do something!

00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:09.000
Knock-on.

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:12.290
I-I'm sorry.

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:15.450
Calm down. It's fine.

00:13:15.450 --> 00:13:17.120
Snap out of it and let's go!

00:13:25.580 --> 00:13:27.950
Koufuuin's ball.

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:30.370
What a let down, Ibuki.

00:13:33.410 --> 00:13:35.410
You didn't meet my expectations at all.

00:13:37.910 --> 00:13:39.830
What?

00:13:41.870 --> 00:13:43.790
You're in the way, shorty.

00:13:45.450 --> 00:13:47.870
Shit! Shit!

00:13:47.870 --> 00:13:49.120
Kotori-<i>chan</i>.

00:13:56.830 --> 00:13:58.200
We did it!

00:13:58.200 --> 00:14:00.200
I love you, Ishigami-<i>senpai</i>!

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:12.500
I'll distract them, so get a try.

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:13.750
That's right.

00:14:13.750 --> 00:14:17.700
There's no reason to make up
for my size just because I'm small.

00:14:17.700 --> 00:14:20.950
I was able to get this far because of my size!

00:14:20.950 --> 00:14:23.540
There are things I can do because of it!

00:14:23.540 --> 00:14:24.950
I'll show them.

00:14:24.950 --> 00:14:30.620
I'll show everyone who looked down on me!

00:14:30.620 --> 00:14:33.830
Take that!

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:37.450
We did it!

00:14:37.450 --> 00:14:41.750
Ha, ha. You got fooled.

00:14:41.750 --> 00:14:43.450
Don't get cocky.

00:14:47.830 --> 00:14:50.620
He gave you quite a glare.

00:14:50.620 --> 00:14:52.330
What did you do, Natsusa?

00:14:52.330 --> 00:14:56.700
Me? I did exactly what you
told me to do, Taku-<i>senpai</i>.

00:14:56.750 --> 00:14:57.830
"Yamamoto Central Hospital"

00:14:57.830 --> 00:14:59.500
"Yamamoto Central Hospital"
Oh, that's completely pointless.

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:05.250
But if someone like you, who has
taken care of Kotori, explains it to him...

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:06.540
It's no use.

00:15:06.540 --> 00:15:10.750
Kotori won't listen to anyone at this point.

00:15:10.750 --> 00:15:12.750
Is that so?

00:15:12.750 --> 00:15:13.750
Right.

00:15:13.750 --> 00:15:17.870
A lot of players in our position
have troublesome personalities.

00:15:17.870 --> 00:15:19.950
A lot of them have complexes about their size.

00:15:19.950 --> 00:15:22.620
It's fine for accepting people like me,

00:15:22.620 --> 00:15:27.790
but most players in our position
want to play a different one.

00:15:27.790 --> 00:15:30.950
Kotori wanted to become a number 8.

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:33.700
That's why he's always so aggressive.

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:36.290
That's the problem.

00:15:36.290 --> 00:15:42.330
That weird pride of his
and the pressure to fill your shoes

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:44.580
is destroying him.

00:15:44.580 --> 00:15:47.250
He'll self-destruct at the match at this rate.

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:49.540
It's fine to let him self-destruct.

00:15:49.540 --> 00:15:50.700
Huh?

00:15:50.700 --> 00:15:53.700
The bigger the explosion, the better.

00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:56.580
You should just provoke
the hell out of him, Natsusa.

00:15:56.580 --> 00:15:58.040
What? Provoke him?

00:15:58.040 --> 00:16:02.330
I'm not very good at saying things
to people that they don't want to hear...

00:16:03.660 --> 00:16:07.080
Looks like I've damaged my eardrum, too.

00:16:07.080 --> 00:16:10.250
You're not hearing things, Taku-<i>senpai</i>.

00:16:11.580 --> 00:16:14.080
That was a good use of your muscles!

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:19.500
Goodness. He hates me now
because of you, Taku-<i>senpai</i>.

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:20.500
Now?

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:21.580
Hey!

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:24.200
Bro. Sorry. I let my guard down.

00:16:24.200 --> 00:16:25.410
No, no.

00:16:25.410 --> 00:16:29.950
You were supposed to be marking Ibuki,
so you didn't do anything wrong.

00:16:29.950 --> 00:16:33.410
He'll only be able to do something
like that once a match.

00:16:33.410 --> 00:16:37.540
And we'll be able to see
Shingyouji's conversion kick now!

00:16:37.540 --> 00:16:39.750
That's what you wanted to see, right?

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:44.200
Try your best!

00:16:47.120 --> 00:16:49.040
That's right, Sei!

00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:53.620
I thought of this when we went to Oita,
but you should set a routine!

00:16:53.620 --> 00:16:55.000
Routine?

00:16:55.000 --> 00:16:58.330
Something you always do
right before a conversion kick!

00:16:58.330 --> 00:17:00.160
Madoka-<i>san </i>has one, right?

00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:02.830
He looks at the goal and smiles!

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:05.410
Even a famous player like that has one!

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:07.580
We should think of one for you, Sei.

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:09.830
They say it helps you stabilize!

00:17:09.830 --> 00:17:11.080
Then, you do it.

00:17:11.080 --> 00:17:12.450
Huh?

00:17:12.450 --> 00:17:14.410
You should smile.

00:17:14.410 --> 00:17:16.290
Me?

00:17:16.290 --> 00:17:18.000
That's right.

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:19.540
You want me to smile?

00:17:19.540 --> 00:17:22.200
Right before your conversion kick?

00:17:22.200 --> 00:17:23.330
That's right.

00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:24.790
Isn't that weird?

00:17:24.790 --> 00:17:27.700
It's not. You do it.

00:17:27.700 --> 00:17:29.660
Well, I don't mind.

00:17:29.660 --> 00:17:32.160
Hopefully I can do it well...

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:34.000
Practice before the match.

00:17:34.000 --> 00:17:37.790
You're definitely giving me acting advice!

00:17:37.790 --> 00:17:40.040
<i>Amenbo akaina </i>A-I-U-E-O!

00:17:40.040 --> 00:17:41.620
What are you doing so suddenly?!

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:44.540
I'm stretching the muscles around my mouth!

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:46.750
Natsusa-<i>san</i>, do you need a mirror?!

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:49.080
N-No! I-I'll be fine!

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:50.450
I'll get nervous if I look!

00:17:50.450 --> 00:17:52.660
I'm already really nervous!

00:17:52.660 --> 00:17:53.830
What should I do?!

00:17:53.830 --> 00:17:57.950
C-Calm down! Do you need
some sports drink? Oxygen?!

00:17:57.950 --> 00:18:00.410
--What in the world are you two doing?
--Make sure to breathe!

00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:06.580
What a funny face.

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:21.000
He's so stable!

00:18:28.450 --> 00:18:30.160
Thank goodness.

00:18:30.160 --> 00:18:31.700
Yeah.

00:18:31.700 --> 00:18:34.500
But now I feel nauseous
from all that nervousness.

00:18:34.500 --> 00:18:35.910
What's going on?

00:18:37.950 --> 00:18:38.870
Again!

00:18:38.870 --> 00:18:40.700
I won't fall for the same trick twice!

00:18:45.830 --> 00:18:47.040
High tackle!

00:18:48.330 --> 00:18:49.660
Sorry, Ikuto.

00:18:49.660 --> 00:18:50.910
Are you all right?

00:18:50.910 --> 00:18:52.000
Yeah.

00:18:52.000 --> 00:18:55.790
Sorry, this guy is still pretty new at rugby.

00:18:55.790 --> 00:18:58.370
Touma! Apologize!

00:18:58.370 --> 00:19:00.580
I'm sorry.

00:19:01.580 --> 00:19:04.790
We're very sorry! Really!

00:19:04.790 --> 00:19:06.450
I'm sorry.

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:09.500
Only a warning this time.

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:10.540
Be careful from now on.

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:11.950
Yes.

00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:14.870
You're good...

00:19:14.870 --> 00:19:16.830
Hm? What do you mean?

00:19:16.830 --> 00:19:18.450
Again!

00:19:18.450 --> 00:19:22.200
Zaitsu-<i>san </i>is really bad at things like that...

00:19:25.330 --> 00:19:26.290
Zaitsu-<i>senpai</i>.

00:19:26.290 --> 00:19:27.620
Hm?

00:19:27.620 --> 00:19:29.500
I'd like a place kick.

00:19:31.910 --> 00:19:34.910
Got it. Give it a try.

00:19:37.290 --> 00:19:39.200
Place kick, please.

00:19:39.200 --> 00:19:41.290
--Place kick.
--Huh? What?!

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:43.750
A penalty kick from a place like that?!

00:19:43.750 --> 00:19:45.040
Huh? Really?

00:19:45.040 --> 00:19:47.410
Even for Sei, isn't that really hard?

00:19:47.410 --> 00:19:48.910
You're so noisy, Natsusa...

00:20:09.500 --> 00:20:11.200
How beautiful!

00:20:14.910 --> 00:20:16.450
It went in...

00:20:18.370 --> 00:20:20.790
It went in!

00:20:20.790 --> 00:20:21.620
Yuu...

00:20:21.620 --> 00:20:22.660
Yes!

00:20:22.660 --> 00:20:25.870
Give me a bag, my nerves are making me sick...

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:28.120
--Huh?!
--Y-Yes!

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:31.750
Good job.

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:33.750
You got your touch back!

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:38.450
By the way, is Natsusa all right?

00:20:48.250 --> 00:20:51.870
Madoka-<i>san</i>. Sorry about earlier.

00:20:51.870 --> 00:20:53.450
It seems I did something wrong.

00:20:53.450 --> 00:20:55.870
Not at all. Not at all.

00:20:55.870 --> 00:20:57.500
Keep doing what you're doing.

00:20:57.500 --> 00:20:59.080
Don't hold back.

00:20:59.080 --> 00:21:05.620
Just tackle a little lower next time.
Then it'll be perfect.

00:21:05.620 --> 00:21:07.290
Yes.

00:21:07.290 --> 00:21:09.790
Okay! I'm counting on you!

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:17.620
What's the point if you quit rugby?

00:21:22.330 --> 00:21:23.870
Don't run away!

00:21:23.870 --> 00:21:27.040
Quit aiming for Ibuki all the time
and fight me head-on!

00:21:27.040 --> 00:21:28.700
You aren't an enemy to me.

00:21:28.700 --> 00:21:30.200
What?!

00:21:30.200 --> 00:21:35.040
I said a man without any skill like you
isn't worth shit to me.

00:21:35.040 --> 00:21:35.950
Go to hell!

00:21:35.950 --> 00:21:37.040
Hey! Stop it!

00:21:37.040 --> 00:21:39.700
--You do not have the Japanese spirit?!
--Calm down, Ethan!

00:21:39.700 --> 00:21:42.200
"Last half"

00:21:52.500 --> 00:21:55.660
Jeez! Kazutaka-<i>san </i>is just so persistent!

00:21:55.660 --> 00:21:59.200
Ibuki hasn't gotten any
chances to touch the ball.

00:21:59.200 --> 00:22:03.040
Because of that, they can
easily read our attacks...

00:22:08.580 --> 00:22:11.080
Doushisha. Number 10. Bleeding injury.

00:23:41.950 --> 00:23:46.000
"You Can Do It! JAPAN Rugby!!!"

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:46.910
"You Can Do It! JAPAN Rugby!!!"
Watch it.
